### The one row worth a second look: the posture on `src`

`src/` holds `main.py` and nothing else — the project's own code, no vendored platform or framework core. Two files in the framework point opposite ways on that case:

- `new-project.md` says a folder holding code *a platform or framework updates* takes `Repository`, and **"anything else takes `Assets`."** Read literally, `src` takes `Assets`.
- Decision `0006` says that in "a folder of the project's own code with no vendored core, both words behave identically today", and keeps `Repository` as the word carrying the layer "expected to grow".

I propose `Repository`, because the behaviour is identical today and the word will still be right when the folder grows a dependency it does not hand-edit. `Assets` on a source folder reads as an error to anyone who opens the registry. Say the word and I will switch it.

